    {
      "id": "cae48ee4-7f58-465d-a826-6611447dc189",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -300,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 1000,
        "content": "## Collect quote requests in Google Sheets and ask for missing details\n\nFor small service businesses (movers, cleaners, contractors, installers) that quote jobs by email and keep track in Google Sheets.\n\n### How it works\n1. A customer fills the quote request form.\n2. The workflow checks the details you need to quote and saves the request in Google Sheets as `ready_to_quote` or `missing_info`.\n3. You get an email with the request at `owner_email`.\n4. The customer gets an email right away: a confirmation, or a short list of what is missing.\n\n### Setup\n1. In Google Sheets, create a tab named `Requests`. Paste the column line from the **Sheet** note into cell A1, then Data > Split text to columns.\n2. Open **Already received?** and **Save request**: pick your Google Sheets credential and paste your sheet URL in **Document**.\n3. Open **Email the owner**, **Ask for missing details** and **Confirm request**: pick your Gmail credential. All emails go out from that Gmail account.\n4. Edit **Settings** (set `business_name` and `owner_email` first) and the service options in **Quote request form**.\n5. Test: click Execute workflow, open the Test URL and send a request with your own email.\n6. Activate and share the **Production URL** of **Quote request form**.\n\nIf nothing happens, open **Executions** to see the error.\n\n### Requirements\n- Google Sheets and Gmail credentials in n8n: docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/credentials/google/. If your Google Cloud app is in Testing mode, the connection expires after 7 days; publish the app to avoid it.\n\n### Customization\n- Change what you receive in **Email the owner**, and what customers receive in **Ask for missing details** and **Confirm request**.\n\nBuilt and tested by Small Hours, a team of AI agents."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "169b9b5b-059e-44f2-a710-f91edff1df78",
      "name": "Sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        860,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "### Sheet: tab named `Requests`\nPaste this line in cell A1, then Data > Split text to columns:\n`request_id,received_at,status,name,email,phone,service,address,preferred_date,details,missing_fields,quote_id,quote_amount,thread_id,quote_sent_at,follow_ups_sent,last_follow_up_at,reply_label,job_start,event_id,closed_at`\n\nThis workflow fills the first 11 columns. Keep the rest: the booking and weekly summary templates use the same sheet. If you only use this one, leave them empty."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f37cd7c5-934b-48e8-afa2-a7109b6bd559",
